WEBVTT

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:05.460
Itagaki has never been able to get past Kuroda.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.630
Itagaki's strengths; slipping past the backline...

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:15.620
...and one-on-one techniques have totally failed against Kuroda.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:21.380
If Kuroda is able to mark him out, Itagaki is practically useless.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.580
Not yet. It's still not the time to leave my position.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:29.560
Just a little bit more... Keep it there.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.710
Now!

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:34.060
See that?

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.990
That's a pity. Still, not bad, Itagaki!

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:51.760
Sera!

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:54.770
Are you alright?

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:47.620
Damn, if only I've been playing on the right side instead...

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:49.820
Itagaki.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.820
Remind yourself why I've decided to choose you.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:03.410
I wouldn't have chosen you if you could only play on the right wing.

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:11.390
I'm a professional manager, and this is how you will be assessed upon.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:17.390
If you are truly a professional, then let me see you live up to my expectations.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:19.440
Understood?

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:23.320
I am trying to bring out your full potential.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.270
Don't think that you can only play well in one aspect.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:29.980
Yes.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:32.870
All of their play goes through Zelberto.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:36.260
Murakoshi, stick close to him.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:43.890
You're working very hard, Tatsumi.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.940
Carlos, that was a good tackle. Keep it up.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:51.090
How can they allow a manager to coach a team without a single foreigner?

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:57.100
There has to be someone who misunderstood the meaning of the word 'professional'.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:04:03.040
All they fancy is the title of their position. In reality, they don't even have a clue of what to do.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:07.960
Are you watching, Chairman Nagata?

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:15.040
My management team are doing their best so that I would be able to build an ideal team.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.610
They never take 'impossible' as an answer.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:21.270
The board,

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:22.630
coaches,

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:23.580
and players.

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:29.150
All of them must be able to fulfill all obligations.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.530
That is what I deem as an ideal football club.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:38.060
I will bring them to the top.

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:42.570
Sera's back on the pitch!

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.740
That's a relief.

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:49.020
We're done for if our strikers miss out.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.450
That said though, we didn't even have a sniff at the opponent's goal.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:58.650
Is this match going to be fine?

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:02.140
We can't win if all we do is defend.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:14.870
All he talks about is his ideals, and he never took reality into perspective. What can someone like him achieve?

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:17.430
Tatsumi.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.900
Let them see the potential of ETU.

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:31.090
There's always space for Itagaki to work with.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.590
Guess I'll pass it to him...

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:43.400
...not.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:53.280
Don't let him dribble!

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.410
Put him off! Disrupt his momentum.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:57.790
Sekine!

00:05:58.840 --> 00:05:59.800
To the side?

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:01.770
Shit!

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.170
What are you doing, Tanba?

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:13.580
If he's marking you,

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:19.060
it should be a cinch right, Pepe?

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:23.860
It's Pepe.

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:43.130
Tsubaki...

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:44.490
Great block!

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:47.540
Nice save, Tsubaki!

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:50.450
Are you alright?

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:54.520
Tsubaki?

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.400
That was close!

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:07.270
If the team had conceded because of me again, I think I'm toast.

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:09.040
That's true.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:15.800
I feel a little dizzy. And my ear's buzzing too.

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:17.550
I bet.

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:21.700
Murakoshi! Tanba! Focus!

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:25.690
Tsubaki actually did a crucial contribution while we were in a pinch.

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:29.750
Thanks to Tsubaki's simple-mindedness, we're saved.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:36.130
I instructed him to run to the end of the line when Pepe is in a one-on-one situation, but...

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:39.930
That was certainly perfect timing.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:42.920
It could have easily been an own goal.

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:46.430
Still, he did it without hesitation.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:50.750
Great judgment, Tsubaki. I can see he's finally concentrating.

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:59.330
Good, nice clear!

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.990
We've been constantly under siege for this game.

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:08.010
That's fine.

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:12.030
As long as we don't concede.

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:19.980
Fifteen minutes left in the first half.

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:23.380
Nagoya is dominating possession.

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:28.510
Zelberto and Pepe brought the ball towards goal just then.

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:32.920
Even if ETU is a defensive-minded team like last year,

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:36.520
it's only a matter of time before they concede, isn't it?

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:44.550
What's truly intriguing is that Tsubaki has been playing without fear.

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:54.540
Though he's still running around like a headless chicken and couldn't catch up with Carlos,

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:02.860
he does play as if he has a purpose on the pitch.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:06.490
No, it's not just Tsubaki.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:18.130
The whole ETU team is giving off the exact same aura.

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:21.390
If I am right about this,

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:26.380
then ETU definitely has a plan.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:31.510
ETU will start to get their game going when it reaches a certain period.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:42.190
Does this team actually plan to attack?

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:45.470
Why do they keep focusing their passes here?

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:50.810
I'll take this route then.

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:53.310
Good. Let's get this going!

00:09:53.690 --> 00:10:00.510
Is there any fun in parking the bus? You don't score if you don't shoot!

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:07.200
Hey. Get past me if you can, dumbass!

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.590
You're noisy, Kuroda.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:12.590
They're attacking up the flank!

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:15.990
Stick to him, Ishihama!

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:20.180
It's a header!

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:22.760
Pick up the second ball!

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:24.030
Zelberto!

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:29.170
Cut off his pass!

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:41.600
That lad...

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:43.060
Nice!

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:47.050
Let's attack the flanks once more!

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:51.010
You guys have to hold on!

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:54.590
Just a little more...

00:11:32.390 --> 00:11:34.100
0-0 at half time.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:36.520
We made it, somehow.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:46.990
My ears are finally back to normal.

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:54.160
Wh-What's this?

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:58.250
Is he trying to challenge me?

00:11:58.640 --> 00:12:00.900
H-Hello!

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:04.260
Pepe is complimenting you!

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.720
You're fearless, flying into two shots like that.

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:11.270
Great bravery there.

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:16.890
W-What's this? I can't grasp a thing they're saying.

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:20.150
I say, Zelberto!

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:23.700
Those are our names printed on the flags!

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:25.660
Huh? What're you talking about?

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:27.910
It's true!

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:31.290
I wish I could take a picture.

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:37.120
W-What's with those guys?

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:46.970
That performance just now...

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:54.430
I won't let you do that later.

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:05.890
Dammit.

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:15.160
When I was still a rookie, there was this amazing forward in Nagoya called Domingo.

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:21.310
Because of his searing pace and unique dribbling style, he could completely change a game by himself.

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:28.120
I was quite upset.

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:33.390
That was the most embarrassing incident of my career.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:37.440
From then on,

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:41.010
I started to immerse myself in studying Domingo's moves.

00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:43.150
And then...

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:49.180
When ETU got promoted, and I was about to kick Domingo's butt,

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.530
Domingo...

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:58.340
...returned to Colombia.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:01.710
Why the sudden gibbering?

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:05.500
We only praised you for having great morale.

00:14:08.020 --> 00:14:11.690
That bastard Itagaki learnt quite a lot from Domingo.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:18.830
Itagaki's play... It's like the exact copy of Domingo's style.

00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:22.620
No, I should say it's a fake copy of Domingo's.

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:25.770
He couldn't even get past me.

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:34.870
I had loads of time when I was unmarked, but...

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:37.840
Damn!

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:39.420
My...

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:42.490
...potential?

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:48.750
Stay where you are and listen.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:52.500
We were dominating during the first half,

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:56.260
and the game will be ours if we sustain our momentum in the second half.

00:14:56.980 --> 00:14:59.680
However, you guys should notice that we have too few shots on goal.

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:03.470
We need to pass more intricately and complete more of our attacks.

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:09.020
The opponent's defense isn't impregnable.

00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:12.550
If we play to our usual game, we'll win.

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:14.540
The manager's right.

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:16.200
It'll be alright.

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:19.540
Victory will come to those who enjoy football the most.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:22.670
Isn't that right? Carlos? Pepe?

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:28.590
Pepe, what's that you're eating?

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:31.390
There's still the second half!

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:37.090
Alright! We need to stamp our authority on the pitch during the second half!

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:40.320
Great, let's go!

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:41.040
Yeah!

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:45.680
The atmosphere here is great.

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:50.000
The team's morale can greatly boost a player's confidence.

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:54.000
Do you have any plans for the second half, Tatsumi?

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:57.540
If you've decided to initiate attack, try it then.

00:15:59.570 --> 00:16:02.200
We'll cut you down.

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:12.550
The atmosphere is really tense.

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:17.270
Uhh...

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:19.080
Nothing to comment on.

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:24.200
Uhh... manager?

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:29.120
The second half should be played just like the first, is that it?

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:31.900
That's right.

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:36.720
That's because I've already told you my plan for the entire game before the match.

00:16:37.070 --> 00:16:40.230
That's not it. The problem lies in the way you talk to others.

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:44.870
You should just play like you did in the first half. The line-up will be unchanged.

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:55.500
Alright, make them cower in fear!

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:01.900
Kudou!

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:05.790
Which team's gonna score first in the second half?

00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:08.790
That's classified information.

00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:14.100
It's going to unravel soon anyway. I think it's going to be either Zelberto or Pepe.

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:20.610
To take a good picture, one has to search for signs on the pitch.

00:17:23.740 --> 00:17:25.650
Trust your own instincts.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.290
That's what it takes to be a cameraman.

00:17:31.990 --> 00:17:35.150
We were utterly dominated by the opponents during the first half.

00:17:36.510 --> 00:17:40.280
Because of Tsubaki's performance, we were able to hold on, but...

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:45.550
It's a matter of time till we concede in the second half.

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:53.500
If that happens, it will be six straight losses since the start of the season. Will it be okay?

00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:24.450
The supporters are still believing...

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:30.120
And as the PR of the team, how could I not believe in the team too?

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:38.470
They broke through down the flank!

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:40.650
Here.

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:44.860
The defense's tight!

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:45.990
The opponent's countering!

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:47.350
Zelberto!

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:48.750
Here!

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:51.860
Great, Murakoshi!

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:54.860
This guy...

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:56.500
Reclaim the ball!

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:06.320
Pass it to me!

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:09.460
How is this? There are no open players!

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:12.210
Sekine! Wait for assistance from the flanks!

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:18.200
Too high!

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:20.820
Let's keep it going!

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:24.870
We need to raise our game!

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:33.490
Being pressured into their own half from the start of the second half... That's bad, ETU.

00:19:34.550 --> 00:19:37.470
Your words will be misunderstood! You're incredulous!

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:39.450
Which side are you really on?!

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:42.040
I'm sorry.

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:46.150
It's because the opponents are piling on the attack, while we're defending for our lives.

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:51.630
Murakoshi, who was getting toyed around during the first half, has finally grasped Zelberto's movements.

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:54.860
Sugie haven't allowed Pepe to deal any real damage too.

00:19:56.410 --> 00:19:59.390
Theoretically, the only worry now is...

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:02.300
...the space in front of Itagaki.

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:06.780
That area had been constantly exploited by the opponents in the first half.

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:12.070
It was not really being exploited, since we were actually allowing them to exploit it.

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:15.790
If there's space to pass to, then others would naturally want to exploit it.

00:20:16.510 --> 00:20:19.910
More so, if the opponent's philosophy is similar to that of this season's Nagoya.

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:26.170
When you know where your enemy will attack from, defending against them would be a cinch.

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:30.650
Additionally, we have Itagaki's nemesis, Kuroda, boxing him out.

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:35.550
I sure hope we can maintain our shape for the second half.

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:39.430
If we can, then there will be chances for us to pounce on.

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:47.540
Damn, he's sticking to me like chewing gum.

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:57.150
But still, it doesn't affect me much at all.

00:20:58.930 --> 00:21:00.950
Furthermore, I'm still able to pass a ball like this.

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:04.740
No matter how many times you do it, the result will be the same-

00:21:05.420 --> 00:21:06.320
Ishiyama, get him!

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:07.840
This doesn't look good!

00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:11.590
If...

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:14.090
...we don't convert our chances,

00:21:17.090 --> 00:21:19.610
Stop him!

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:21.590
Will he shoot?

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:23.110
Or pass?

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:39.110
Tsubaki!

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:40.890
Nice block!

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:42.600
Good work!

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:49.270
That kid may be useless at times, but he can really stand out during the most crucial moments!

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:54.060
I can't take this any longer. I'm already having goosebumps!

00:21:55.030 --> 00:21:55.760
Tsubaki...

00:21:56.270 --> 00:22:00.230
Nice, Tsubaki! Great run!

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:02.240
Yes!

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:04.820
Not too shabby.

00:22:05.860 --> 00:22:06.870
What are you referring to?

00:22:07.990 --> 00:22:10.880
That kid. He's everywhere.

00:22:11.750 --> 00:22:15.500
Great judgment there, Tsubaki! You bastard!

00:22:16.650 --> 00:22:18.660
Kuroda, is that what you call 'praising'?

00:22:25.800 --> 00:22:28.800
I haven't stop running the entire match.

00:22:30.880 --> 00:22:31.760
Huh?

00:22:35.600 --> 00:22:37.930
Mark your man! Concentrate!

00:22:47.450 --> 00:22:48.100
Huh?

00:22:49.900 --> 00:22:51.280
The stadium...

00:22:52.880 --> 00:22:54.750
...gives off a feeling like this?

00:24:15.360 --> 00:24:16.400
Watch out!

00:24:16.400 --> 00:24:17.230
Okay!

00:24:17.230 --> 00:24:19.520
Everything got stopped by them!

00:24:20.650 --> 00:24:22.110
So they've noticed.

00:24:22.130 --> 00:24:28.480
Twenty minutes left. This is the point that separates the contenders from the pretenders.
